/**
 * The addresses of the Internet Protocol as values: an IPv4 address, an IPv6 address, an address of either version, and
 * a socket address - an address and a port. Each is read from text and shown as text (RFC 5952 for IPv6), compared and
 * hashed like any other value.
 *
 * `std/ip` touches nothing: it has no natives and needs no capability, so a package that only names an address - a URI
 * with an IP literal host, a configuration file - does not claim the network by importing it. `std/network` connects to
 * these addresses and re-exports every name of this package (docs/design/URI.md section 8a).
 *
 *     const local = SocketAddress(IpAddress.loopback, 8080)
 *     print local
 */

public use AddressError, Ipv4Address, Ipv6Address, IpAddress, SocketAddress from "./address"
